# hypernix.coffee_maker

3 training tiers: drip / french_press / percolator + cold_brew for long checkpointed runs.

## Documentation pages

- [CoffeeMaker](../../#/docs/CoffeeMaker) · [MDXL source](pages/CoffeeMaker.mdxl)

## API reference

[Open the API reference source](pages/api-reference.mdxl)

### `Brew()`

One result from a single ``brew_fn()`` call.

### `CoffeeMaker()`

Repeat ``brew_fn`` on an interval.

### `CoffeeMaker.run(cycles) -> list[Brew]`

Run exactly ``cycles`` brews (sleeping between them).

### `CoffeeMaker.serve(install_sigint=True) -> list[Brew]`

Run until :meth:`stop` is called. If ``install_sigint`` is

### `CoffeeMaker.stop() -> None`

Cooperative cancel. Finishes the current brew, then exits.

### `FrenchPressMaker()`

Batch brew: takes a list of callables, runs them all once,

### `PercolatorMaker()`

Cyclic brew: the output of cycle N is passed as the input to

### `ColdBrewMaker()`

Long-running single brew with mandatory disk checkpoints.

